acpi2dt - licensing
===================

acpi2dt combines its own source code with third-party code. Every source
file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier; the full license texts are in
LICENSES/.

Source code
-----------

  acpi2dt/src, acpi2dt/inc            MIT (LICENSES/MIT)
    except acpi2dt/src/pdc_maps.c     GPL-2.0-only (LICENSES/GPL-2.0)
                                      - data taken from the Linux kernel
                                        (drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-x1e80100.c)

  acpi2dt/third_party/acpica          BSD-3-Clause OR GPL-2.0-only
                                      (Intel ACPICA, LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause,
                                      LICENSES/GPL-2.0)
  acpi2dt/third_party/dtc             GPL-2.0-or-later (dtc compiler)
    libfdt/ headers                   GPL-2.0-or-later OR BSD-2-Clause
    getopt.c / getopt.h               MIT (musl libc)
    unistd.h, dtc_port.h              MIT (Windows port glue)

  See third_party/README.md for origin, versions and local modifications.

The acpi2dt.exe binary
----------------------

acpi2dt.exe links the embedded dtc compiler (GPL-2.0-or-later) and
pdc_maps.c (GPL-2.0-only). The binary as a whole is therefore distributed
under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 2 only
(GPL-2.0-only); ACPICA is used under its GPL-2.0-only option (or its
GPL-compatible BSD-3-Clause option) and the MIT parts are GPL-compatible.
Whoever distributes the binary must offer the corresponding source code
(this repository) under GPL-2.0.

The MIT licensed files remain usable under MIT on their own.

Other projects of the solution
------------------------------

acpica/, dtc/ and libyaml/ next to acpi2dt/ are separate projects and keep
their own licenses (ACPICA: BSD-3-Clause OR GPL-2.0-only, dtc:
GPL-2.0-or-later, libyaml: MIT).

Firmware
--------

Firmware files that acpi2dt copies from the Windows DriverStore are not part
of acpi2dt and are usually not redistributable.
